       On success, ggeettpprriioorriittyy() returns  the  calling  thread’s  nice  value,
       which may be a negative number.  On error, it returns -1 and sets _e_r_r_n_o
       to indicate the error.

       Since  a  successful  call to ggeettpprriioorriittyy() can legitimately return the
       value -1, it is necessary to clear _e_r_r_n_o prior to the call, then  check
       _e_r_r_n_o afterward to determine if -1 is an error or a legitimate value.

       sseettpprriioorriittyy() returns 0 on success.  On failure, it returns -1 and sets
       _e_r_r_n_o to indicate the error.

